From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:53:56 +0900
Subject: Give an uninitialized ContextBase the default fuel for recursive
 operations
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The operations `handleRecursive` tracks are kept in an array on the context
base whose length is the limit on their depth. `ContextBase.initialize` sizes
it from `-Xmax-fuel` (550 by default), but until then it had ten slots, "so a
few calls to handleRecursive work for trivial things before the compiler has
really started". A base that is never initialized, such as one made only to
parse source and traverse the trees, therefore threw RecursionOverflow at the
eleventh nested tree: folding over `1 + 2 + … + 12` was enough.

The array now starts at the setting's default, so such a base has the room for
recursion that a compiler run with no `-Xmax-fuel` has.

Written with LLM assistance (Claude Code); reviewed content.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Proscala-Patch: fuelslots
---
 compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/core/Contexts.scala | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/core/Contexts.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/core/Contexts.scala
index c2ad40caae23260d8f10eebf4037609fbc2a97fd..9b490bcb1bfce1ce7f8405e5384af9a343272306 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/core/Contexts.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/core/Contexts.scala
@@ -1070,11 +1070,13 @@ object Contexts {
      */
     private[dotc] var coverage: Coverage | Null = null
 
-    // The array will be initialized with a number of slots corresponding to the max fuel,
-    // for now give it 10 slots so a few calls to handleRecursive work for trivial things
-    // before the compiler has really started
+    // The array has a number of slots corresponding to the max fuel: the configured one
+    // once `initialize` has run, and the default until then, so that a base which is never
+    // initialized (one made only to parse and traverse trees, say) has the same room for
+    // recursion as a compiler run with no `-Xmax-fuel`.
     private[dotc] var recursiveDepth: Int = 0
-    private[dotc] var recursiveOperations: Array[RecursiveOperation] = Array.fill(10)(RecursiveOperation.blank())
+    private[dotc] var recursiveOperations: Array[RecursiveOperation] =
+      Array.fill(ScalaSettings.XmaxFuel.valueIn(ScalaSettings.defaultState))(RecursiveOperation.blank())
 
     // Types state
     /** A table for hash consing unique types */
